From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BDK Patches <patches@bdk.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:16:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] bdk: let an embedder supply the screen capture ui

getDisplayMedia() and chrome.desktopCapture.chooseDesktopMedia() show a
source picker (DesktopMediaPickerImpl or ShareThisTabMediaPicker) and,
while a page shares, a notification (ScreenCaptureNotificationUIImpl for a
screen or a window, TabSharingUI for a tab). All are views UI. An embedder
whose windows are not views widgets cannot parent them: the picker is a
tab-modal dialog that failed a check and ended the process, so BDK refused
every getDisplayMedia() call (BDK task T-UIR-13).

Add embedder_screen_capture_ui.h, a small inline header with two factories
an embedder sets once before any page asks to capture (no new target, as
embedder_prompt_visibility.h). DesktopMediaPicker::Create returns the
embedder's picker when it has one, and GetDevicesForDesktopCapture asks the
embedder for the notification of every capture it would show one for.
Everything else of the capture path is unchanged: the access handler, the
source lists the picker is given, the stream, the capture indicator and
its policy checks. With no factory set nothing changes. Only the two .cc
files and the new header are touched.

Used by: the BDK engine (//bdk/engine/ui_screen_capture.cc).
